  "context_pill": "Corporate Taxation | Marginal Relief",
  "example_summary": "Computation of Marginal Relief for X Ltd. for A.Y.2026-27 when total income exceeds ₹ 1 crore.",
  "source_provision": "| Category | Surcharge Threshold | Marginal Relief Applicability |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Total Income > ₹ 1 Crore | 7% | Applicable |\n| Total Income > ₹ 10 Crore | 12% | Applicable |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Marginal Relief Rule: The Income tax plus surcharge on total income shall not exceed the aggregate of income tax on ₹ 1 crore (or ₹ 10 crore) plus the amount by which the total income exceeds ₹ 1 crore (or ₹ 10 crore).\n\n\n**Key Statutory Conditions**\n* Marginal relief is intended to bridge the disparity created by the imposition of a surcharge when total income slightly exceeds the defined threshold.\n* The relief is available only to the extent that the additional tax burden (due to surcharge) exceeds the amount of the income exceeding the threshold.\n\n\n**Tax Calculation Sequence**\n1. Calculate Income Tax on Total Income.\n2. Add Surcharge at the applicable slab rate.\n3. Calculate 'Tax Threshold Limit' (Tax on limit amount + excess income over limit).\n4. If (1+2) > 3, then Tax Payable = 3.",
